# Normalise line endings.
#
# This repo lives on a WSL path and is edited from both Windows and Linux
# tooling. Without this, a save from the Windows side rewrites a whole file
# from LF to CRLF; git then sees every line as changed, which has produced
# 13,000-line diffs containing no actual change and phantom merge conflicts
# across files nobody touched.
#
# `text=auto` tells git to detect text files and store them with LF in the
# repository; `eol=lf` checks them out as LF everywhere, including Windows.
# Modern editors handle LF on Windows without complaint.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never touch these, or they get corrupted.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.zip   binary
*.db    binary
*.sqlite3 binary

# Generated files — collapse them in diffs and exclude from language stats so
# they do not drown out real changes in a review.
package-lock.json  -diff linguist-generated
backend/openapi.yaml linguist-generated
